※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ A generic function's type parameter may be read off a type the call hands it
※ -- `kind: ⌜T'⌝`, called with `⌜A⌝` -- where nothing else the call hands says
※ it, which is what a function answering a different type for each of several
※ asks for.  Nothing is handed at run time.  A condition comparing types
※ (`pre(⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝ ∨ …)`) is settled at the call, before the function is made,
※ and a type it was not meant for is refused there.
※
※ Compare: **Zig**, whose `comptime T: type` parameter this is; **C++**'s
※ explicit template arguments, `make<A>(3)`; **Rust**'s turbofish,
※ `make::<A>(3)`; **Haskell**'s `Proxy` and type applications, `make @A 3`.

type A = n : u8
type B = n : u8
type Kinds = x : u8

fn Kinds.make(kind: ⌜T'⌝, v: u8) → T'
        pre(⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝ ∨ ⌜T'⌝ = ⌜B⌝):
    comptime if ⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝:
        A(.n ← v)
    else:
        B(.n ← v + 1u8)

fn plain(kind: ⌜T'⌝, v: u8) → T':
    comptime if ⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝:
        A(.n ← v)
    else:
        B(.n ← v + 1u8)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let a: A = plain(⌜A⌝, 3u8)
    let b: B = Kinds.make(⌜B⌝, 3u8)
    let c: A = Kinds.make(⌜A⌝, 5u8)
    if a.n = 3u8 ∧ b.n = 4u8 ∧ c.n = 5u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
